{"type":"user","message":{"content":"# Generate Fix Prompt for User Story\n\n## Reference Documentation\n\nRead the following documents to understand context before generating fixes:\n- Read(`./docs/architecture/architecture.yaml`) - architecture_yaml\n- Read(`./docs/product/product.yaml`) - product\n\n## Original User Story\n\n**Story ID:** 96.8\n**Title:** Document Summary On Demand\n\n**As a** Claude User\n**I want** Claude to give me a short summary of a shared Google Doc when I ask for one\n**So that** I can decide whether the document needs my attention without reading it in full\n\n## Current Acceptance Criteria\n1. **AC-1:** Claude must display a summary of 150 words or fewer in the conversation when the Claude User asks for a summary of a shared Google Doc.\n2. **AC-2:** Claude must display the message 'This document is not shared with your account' when the Claude User asks for a summary of a document they cannot access.\n3. **AC-3:** Claude must display the message 'The summary timed out - please try again' when no summary is produced within 30 seconds.\n4. **AC-4:** Claude must state that only the first 10000 words were summarized when the document contains more than 10000 words.\n\n## Validation Failure\n\nThe following check failed and needs to be fixed:\n\n### Failed Check: us-refine/acceptance_criteria\n\n**Question:** For every AC, decide whether its Given/When/Then steps use action\nverbs from the forbidden_actions list in the architecture reference\n(docs/architecture/architecture.yaml).\n\nPass when no AC uses forbidden action verbs in its steps.\nFail when one or more ACs use forbidden action verbs.\n\nContext: emit one line per AC.\n  - \"\u003cAC-id\u003e: ok\"\n  - \"\u003cAC-id\u003e: forbidden verb '\u003cverb\u003e' in \u003cgiven|when|then\u003e\"\n    (e.g. \"AC-2: forbidden verb 'parse' in then\")\n\n**Actual:** fail\n\n**Suggested Fix Template:**\nRewrite each step that uses a forbidden action verb.\n\nUse the vocabulary in the architecture reference to select a concrete\nreplacement verb that specifies the interaction mechanism — not just\nthe user's intent.\n\nAC-1 then step: \"Claude handles the summary request and displays a summary\nof 150 words or fewer in the conversation\" — the verb 'handle' is forbidden\nbecause it hides what the system observably does with the input. Drop\n'handles the summary request' and keep only the observable action.\n\nSuggested rewrite:\n  - then:\n      - Claude displays a summary of 150 words or fewer in the conversation\n(Given: a Google Doc with at least 500 words of body text is shared with the\nClaude User's account; When: the Claude User asks Claude to summarize the\ndocument.)\n\n## Your Task\nAnalyze if you have enough context to generate a confident fix.\n\n**If you can generate a confident fix**, output:\n\n=== FILE_START: tmp/2026-08-15-16-49-38-2443/01-96.8-fix-prompts.md ===\n# Fix Prompt for Story 96.8: Document Summary On Demand\n\n## Instructions\nApply the following changes to the acceptance criteria for this story.\n\n## Original Acceptance Criteria\n1. AC-1: Claude must display a summary of 150 words or fewer in the conversation when the Claude User asks for a summary of a shared Google Doc.\n2. AC-2: Claude must display the message 'This document is not shared with your account' when the Claude User asks for a summary of a document they cannot access.\n3. AC-3: Claude must display the message 'The summary timed out - please try again' when no summary is produced within 30 seconds.\n4. AC-4: Claude must state that only the first 10000 words were summarized when the document contains more than 10000 words.\n\n## Required Changes\n\n### Change #N: [AC-ID]\n**Before:** \u003coriginal description\u003e\n**Issue:** \u003cwhat's wrong with it\u003e\n**After (description):** \u003cone-line rule-based statement with must/should\u003e\n**After (steps):**\n```yaml\n- given:\n    - \"\u003cprecondition\u003e\"\n- when:\n    - \"\u003caction\u003e\"\n- t